<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav December 1996 crude oil imports down.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav December 1996 crude oil imports down.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal statistical office reproted the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV CRUDE OIL IMPORTS	  Dec 96	Nov 96</p>
<p> in tonnes				222,787     294,892</p>
<p> in US$ millions			 39	    56</p>
<p>OIL DERIVATIVES</p>
<p> in tonnes				 18,918	34,310</p>
<p> in US$ millions			  7	    10</p>
<p>NOTES -- Cumulative January-December 1996 crude oil imports stood at 1,321,097 tonnes and were worth $229 million.</p>
<p>Cumulative oil derivates imports for 1996 stood at 1,074,956 and were worth $242 million.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
